  "answer": "# Markdown Briefing\n\n## Key Finding\n**The Calamos/Aksia Private Markets Due Diligence Questionnaire does not specify a maximum single-position size** for a private credit interval fund as a percentage of fund assets in the provided excerpt.\n\n## What the Questionnaire Says\nIn the **Risk Management** section for private credit, the questionnaire asks managers to disclose:\n\n- **How much of the portfolio is expected to be invested in the top 10 positions** as a percentage of fund assets\n- **What the maximum and average position size is** as a percentage of fund assets\n\n## Interpretation\n- The document functions as a **due diligence questionnaire**, not as a prescriptive policy document.\n- It identifies **position concentration** as an important area to assess.\n- However, it **does not provide a numeric cap, required limit, or recommended threshold** for maximum single-position size.\n\n## Answer\n**No maximum single-position size is specified in the provided questionnaire excerpt.**",
